  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the man as a representative of 'most religions'",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man (man) who is depicted with a serious expression and crossed arms, wearing a head covering and beard. This projection occurs because the meme uses the man's appearance — culturally associated with Muslim men — as a visual stand-in for the abstract concept of 'most religions' as stated in the text. The user is implicitly invited to see the man as an exemplar of the peaceful nature of 'most religions', thereby projecting their own understanding or identity onto this visual representation. This projection is reinforced by the textual material ('most religions are religions of peace') which frames the man as a symbol of the generalization.",
